 "title": "Pullback compatibility of the zero locus",
 "statement": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be schemes [def-pc-scheme], let $g:Y\\to X$ be a morphism, and let $M$ and $N$ be invertible $\\mathcal O_X$-modules [def-sc-invertible-module]. For an $\\mathcal O_X$-linear morphism $\\varphi:M\\to N$, one has $\\varphi.zeroLocus.comap\\,g=((\\operatorname{Modules.pullback}\\,g).map\\,\\varphi).zeroLocus$ [def-pc-module-pullback].",
 "source": {
